# Marketing heading typography

When building or editing marketing pages (home sections, solutions, how-it-works, placeholders, future pages):

## Section titles

Use **`h3`** with shared class from `@/lib/typography`:

```tsx
import { sectionHeadingClassName } from "@/lib/typography";

<h3 id="..." className={sectionHeadingClassName}>
  Section title
</h3>
```

Equivalent classes: `text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-2xl`

Do **not** use `text-3xl` / `text-4xl` / `text-5xl` for section headings.

## Item titles (cards, steps, zones, measures)

Use **`h4`** with:

```tsx
import { itemHeadingClassName } from "@/lib/typography";

<h4 className={itemHeadingClassName}>{title}</h4>
```

## Page / hero titles

- **Home hero only** (`HomeHero`): keep the large display `h1` (`text-4xl sm:text-5xl md:text-6xl`). Do not shrink it.
- **Solution product heroes**: `h1` with `solutionHeroHeadingClassName` (`text-2xl sm:text-3xl md:text-4xl`, white on image).
- **Text-only page intros** (e.g. How it works): use the **section** size for the primary title (`sectionHeadingClassName`). Prefer `h1` for SEO on the page title, visually matching the section h3 size.

## Do not

- Reintroduce large `h2` section titles (`text-3xl sm:text-4xl`)
- Nest `h3` item titles under `h3` section titles - demote items to `h4`
